[% if not private %]
The owner (`[[ github_owner ]]`) may push their own work directly to `main` without a PR or passing CI. CI still runs after a push; releases retain their CI gates. Force-push, deletion, and merge commits remain blocked for everyone.

[% if no_ci or no_pr %]
[% if no_pr %]
Pull requests and their review requirements are optional, including for agents. Direct pushes are permitted by this creation policy; history protections still apply.
[% else %]
Other accounts and agents must use squash PRs with resolved review threads, including agents authenticated as the owner.
[% endif %]
[% if no_ci %]
CI is optional as a merge/push requirement. Workflows, security scanning and local bootstrap checks remain enabled; releases retain their CI gates.
[% else %]
Other accounts and agents still require passing, up-to-date GitHub Actions `ci` before publishing, including direct pushes. Agents must not use the owner's bypass.
[% endif %]
GitHub checks the pushing account. Any remaining gate permits only the verified repository owner's bypass.
[% else %]
Other accounts must use a squash PR with passing, up-to-date `ci`. Agents must use PRs and CI even when authenticated as the owner (see `AGENTS.md`). GitHub checks the pushing account, so enforcing a human/agent boundary requires separate credentials.
[% endif %]
[% else %]
GitHub Actions is disabled and no ruleset is installed for this private repo on GitHub Free. Run checks locally. Agents still work on branches and open PRs (see `AGENTS.md`).
[% endif %]
